 "description": "Lower front / nose special armour at ~50 deg (side view): 50 mm exterior steel, four NERA sandwiches (25 mm steel + 12 mm rubber + 10 mm steel) taking about half the volume, 90 mm inner steel (~530 mm thick). The upper glacis above is thin, very sloped steel. Estimates vs long rods ~560-650 mm. Reconstruction from public sources (Tankograd, Below The Turret Ring, Zaloga/Wikipedia, forum analyses); real tank armour is secret. Armour amount = public protection estimate / mass efficiency (NERA ~1.3-1.5, Soviet arrays ~1.17). The explosive inside ERA is an empty gap until explosives are added, and the model under-represents NERA breaking long rods - so a full simulation is penetrated more easily than the real armour; the Tank check uses the estimates. 2D slice.",
